# SAFi Appliance — packages baked into the live rootfs.
#
# EVERY package here is part of the "install" set: live-build snapshots
# chroot.packages.install right after the install pass, diffs it against the
# full chroot package set, and writes the extras to
# binary/live/filesystem.packages-remove. d-i's 14remove-live-packages then
# PURGES every listed package from /target. A package installed only by a
# config/hooks/normal/*.chroot file (after the install pass snapshot) is
# therefore always stripped from the installed disk.
#
# So daemon packages MUST be listed here, even though their postinsts try to
# start services. Service starts are blocked during the build by
# config/includes.chroot_before_packages/usr/sbin/policy-rc.d (copied into the
# chroot before the install pass; removed again by 040-appliance-surface
# before the squashfs is produced), so the build chroot never boots a daemon
# and the installed system gets them intact.
#
# Everything SAFi actually needs at runtime:
#   python3-venv         → virtualenv (DEPLOY_BAREMETAL.md step 4)
#   gcc g++              → a few Python wheels build from source
#   tesseract-ocr-eng    → OCR for image/PDF attachments (Dockerfile ships it)
#   nodejs npm           → npx MCP tool servers (Dockerfile ships Node 22)
#   git                  → waters the repo during PHP-style upgrades (step 10)
#   default-mysql-server → appliance DB (datadir init on first start)
#   mariadb-client       → CLI for that DB
#   apache2              → :443 TLS reverse proxy → browser-setup server
#   certbot              → `safi domain add`: Let's Encrypt certonly via the
#                          Apache plugin (needs DNS + inbound port 80)
#   openssh-server       → operator console access
#   grub-pc              → CRITICAL: the live rootfs becomes /target via the
#                          live-installer. Without grub-install baked in, d-i's
#                          grub-installer falls back to `in-target apt-get
#                          install grub-pc`, which cannot resolve offline and
#                          aborts with "grub-pc failed to install into /target".
#                          grub-pc must therefore be in the rootfs itself.
# Plus the live system needs a kernel/init and tools; live-build supplies the
# base. These are the additions:
apt-utils
apache2
bash
ca-certificates
certbot
cron
curl
dbus
debconf-utils
default-mysql-server
dnsutils
g++
gcc
git
grub-pc
grub-pc-bin
hostname
ifupdown
isc-dhcp-client
less
live-tools
locales
login
mariadb-client
mawk
nano
nodejs
npm
openssh-server
openssl
passwd
procps
plymouth
plymouth-label
plymouth-themes
psmisc
python3-certbot-apache
python3-venv
rsyslog
sudo
tesseract-ocr
tesseract-ocr-eng
wget
